=== Module 12 - Thompson's Construction: RE -> epsilon-NFA ===

regex /a(b|c)/   tree: (cat a (alt b c))
nodes: 5   |regex| (no parens): 4

Thompson NFA:
  states: q0 q1 q2 q3 q4 q5 q6 q7
  alphabet: a b c
  start: q0   accept: q7
  q0 a q1
  q1 epsilon q6
  q2 b q3
  q3 epsilon q7
  q4 c q5
  q5 epsilon q7
  q6 epsilon q2
  q6 epsilon q4
  -> 8 states

runs:  "ab" -> ACCEPT   "ac" -> ACCEPT   "a" -> reject   "abc" -> reject

state count is always <= 2*nodes  (and <= 2*|regex|):
  regex           nodes  chars states   <=2*nodes  <=2*chars 
  /a/                 1      1      2   yes        yes       
  /ab/                3      2      4   yes        yes       
  /a|b/               3      3      6   yes        yes       
  /a*/                2      2      4   yes        yes       
  /(a|b)*/            4      4      8   yes        yes       
  /(a|b)*abb/        10      7     14   yes        yes       
  /a(b|c)*d/          8      6     12   yes        yes       
  /((a|b)(c|d))*/      8      7     14   yes        yes       

full pipeline for /(a|b)*abb/:
  Thompson NFA:            14 states, has epsilon: true
  removeEpsilon():         14 states, has epsilon: false
  L(Thompson NFA) up to length 6:  15 strings
    == L(epsilon-free NFA):        true
    == regex /(a|b)*abb/:          true
    == DFA(Module 10):             true

summary: every regex node -> a fixed-size NFA gadget | NFA states <= 2*nodes always | L(Thompson NFA) == L(regex) == L(DFA)
